\[ \text{Area of semi-circle on } \overline{AB} = \frac{1}{2} \pi a^2 \]

The area of the semi-circle on \( \overline{AC} \) is:
\[ \text{Area of semi-circle on } \overline{AC} = \frac{1}{2} \pi b^2 \]

The area of the semi-circle on \( \overline{CB} \) is:
\[ \text{Area of semi-circle on } \overline{CB} = \frac{1}{2} \pi (a - b)^2 \]

The shaded area is the area of the semi-circle on \( \overline{AB} \) minus the areas of the semi-circles on \( \overline{AC} \) and \( \overline{CB} \):
\[ \text{Shaded area} = \frac{1}{2} \pi a^2 - \frac{1}{2} \pi b^2 - \frac{1}{2} \pi (a - b)^2 \]
