The problem can be approached as a binomial probability problem. If we have 10 buses, each with a probability of 0.1 to not go on the line, then each bus has a probability of 0.9 to go on the line. We need to find the probability that at least 8 buses go on the line, i.e., 8, 9, or all 10 buses go on the line.

