\[ b = -3(-2) = 6. \]

Substitute \(a = -2\) and \(b = 6\) into the first equation:
\[ 1 + (-2) + 6 + c + d = 0 \implies 5 + c + d = 0 \implies c + d = -5. \]

Substitute \(a = -2\) and \(b = 6\) into the second equation:
\[ 4 + 3(-2) + 2(6) + c = 0 \implies 4 - 6 + 12 + c = 0 \implies 10 + c = 0 \implies c = -10. \]
\[ d = -5 - (-10) = 5. \]

So, the coefficients are \(a = -2\), \(b = 6\), \(c = -10\), and \(d = 5\). The expression \(1000a + 100b + 10c + d\) is:
