and its solution \(\left\{ x = 5, y = 10 \right\}\), we can substitute \(x = 5\) and \(y = 10\) into the equations to find \(c_1\) and \(c_2\):

1. \(a_1 \cdot 5 + 10 = c_1 \Rightarrow c_1 = 5a_1 + 10\)
2. \(a_2 \cdot 5 + 10 = c_2 \Rightarrow c_2 = 5a_2 + 10\)

Now we need to solve the new system of equations:
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
a_{1} x + 2 y = a_{1} - c_{1} \\
a_{2} x + 2 y = a_{2} - c_{2}
\end{array}
\right.
\]

Let's substitute \(c_1\) and \(c_2\) into the new system:
1. \(a_1 x + 2y = a_1 - (5a_1 + 10) \Rightarrow a_1 x + 2y = -4a_1 - 10\)
2. \(a_2 x + 2y = a_2 - (5a_2 + 10) \Rightarrow a_2 x + 2y = -4a_2 - 10\)

