If the 2 is in the first position, the digit would need to be followed by 0, 1, 8 and the other four digits could be any combination of the digits 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9. The number of ways to arrange the last six digits is the number of permutations of the multiset {3,4,5,6,7,9} which is the same as 6! (since all six digits are distinct).

