To find the first odd-numbered year after 2006 that has the property, let's first define the property: a year, when split after the third digit, into a three-digit integer and a one-digit integer, must have these two integers a common factor greater than one.

For the year 2007, we split it into 200 and 7. The greatest common divisor (gcd) of 200 and 7 is 1, so 2007 does not have the property. We move on to the next year and continue this check.

To make this systematic, we can write a Python script to check each odd year starting from 2007. We'll split each year into the two parts and calculate their gcd. If the gcd is greater than 1, that year meets the condition.

Let's write the code to find the answer.
