\[ n(n+1) = 3988 \]

Using the quadratic formula \( n = \frac{-1 + \sqrt{1 + 4 \cdot 3988}}{2} \):
\[ n = \frac{-1 + \sqrt{15953}}{2} \approx \frac{-1 + 126.3}{2} \approx 62.65 \]

So, \( n = 62 \) is the largest integer satisfying the inequality. The number of elements up to the 62nd block is:
\[ \frac{62 \cdot 63}{2} = 1953 \]

This means the 62nd block ends at the 1953rd element. The next block (the 63rd block) will be a block of 63 numbers, all of which are odd (since the sequence alternates between odd and even numbers).

