\]
We now need to find the value of \(\frac{3x_1 + 1}{4x_1 - 5} + \frac{3x_2 + 1}{4x_2 - 5} + \frac{3x_3 + 1}{4x_3 - 5}\). Consider the polynomial \(P(x) = (3x+1)Q(x) - 4x^2 - 5x + 1\) where \(Q(x)\) is such that the roots of \(P(x)\) are \(x_1, x_2, x_3\). Since \(x_1, x_2, x_3\) are roots of \(x^3 + 3x + 1 = 0\), we get:
\[
