The result of the division is a large number, and its binary representation contains 152 ones. This means that there are 152 terms in the sum \(2^{a_1} + 2^{a_2} + \ldots + 2^{a_k}\), so \(k = 152\).

The value of \(k\) is \(\boxed{152}\)., ground_truth: 151
