\[ \text{Total Weight} = 125 \times 20 \]

If we want to maximize the number of wrestlers weighing more than 131 kg, we should minimize the weights of the remaining wrestlers. The minimum weight for a sumo wrestler is 90 kg according to the rules. Let's assume the minimum number of wrestlers weigh 90 kg. The rest will weigh more than 131 kg. We can set up the equation to find out the maximum number of wrestlers that can weigh more than 131 kg.

Let \( n \) be the number of wrestlers weighing more than 131 kg. Then \( 20 - n \) is the number of wrestlers weighing 90 kg. The total weight is then given by:
\[ 90(20 - n) + 131n = 2500 \]
Solving this equation will give us the value of \( n \). Let's do this calculation.
</think>

<python>
from sympy import symbols, Eq, solve

