The number of ordered triples \((\ell_A, \ell_B, \ell_C)\) of concurrent qevians is equivalent to the number of ways to choose the intersection point of the cevians, which is the same as choosing the points of tangency of the incircle with the sides of the triangle. Since the points of tangency are fixed for any triangle, there is exactly one such point for each cevian.

