Thus, the maximum length of the horizontal segment is the distance between the points where the cubic equation has roots that are as far apart as possible, which is the distance between the roots \( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} \) and \( \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} \):
\[ \text{Maximum length} = \left| \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} - \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} \right) \right| = \left| \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} \right| = \left| \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3} \right| = \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3} \]

