\]
Since \((\omega^2 - \omega + 1)\omega = \omega^3 - \omega^2 + \omega = 1 - \omega^2 + \omega = 1 - (-1) = 2\), and \(\omega^2 - \omega + 1 = 0\) from \(\omega^2 + \omega + 1 = 0\), we get \(b = 2\).

