A parallelepiped is a polyhedron with 8 vertices. A plane that is equidistant from all 8 vertices of a parallelepiped must be a plane that bisects the parallelepiped into two equal-volume halves. Such a plane must pass through the midpoint of the parallelepiped. There are three such planes: one for each pair of opposite faces. Each of these planes is a median plane of the parallelepiped.

