\[
\boxed{1}
\]

### Part 2: Parallelepiped
A parallelepiped has 8 vertices. A median plane of a parallelepiped is a plane such that the distance from each vertex to the plane is equal. In a parallelepiped, the distance from each vertex to the plane is equal if and only if the plane passes through the centroid of the parallelepiped and is parallel to one of the faces of the parallelepiped. There are 3 such planes, corresponding to the 3 pairs of opposite faces.

