\[\log_{10} \frac{100}{10^{a+1}} < \log_{10} \frac{100}{x} \leq \log_{10} \frac{100}{10^a}\]
\[-(a+1) + \log_{10} 100 < b \leq -a + \log_{10} 100\]
\[-(a+1) + 2 < b \leq -a + 2\]
So, we have:
\[1 - a \leq b \leq 2 - a\]

Since \(b\) is an integer, \(b\) can take values \(1 - a\), \(2 - a\).

Now we want to maximize \(2a^2 - 3b^2\). We will check both possible values of \(b\).

If \(b = 1 - a\), then
\[2a^2 - 3(1 - a)^2 = 2a^2 - 3(1 - 2a + a^2) = 2a^2 - 3 + 6a - 3a^2 = -a^2 + 6a - 3.\]

