This statement is true.

3. \( S_{k+1} = S_k + a_{k+1} \)
This is true because we just showed that the \((k+1)\)-th term is \( a_{k+1} = \frac{1}{3^k} \), and adding this term to the sum of the first \( k \) terms gives the sum of the first \( k+1 \) terms.
\[ S_{k+1} = S_k + \frac{1}{3^k} = S_k + a_{k+1} \]
