Next, we calculate the area of \(\triangle DEF\). Using the coordinates of \(D\), \(E\), and \(F\):
\[
\text{Area of } \triangle DEF = \frac{1}{2} \left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \right|
\]
where \(D = (0, s)\), \(E = \left( \frac{s}{2}, \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}s \right)\), \(F = \left( s, \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}s \right)\).

Plugging these into the formula:
