A tetrahedron has 4 vertices. If a plane is a median plane, the distance from each of the 4 vertices to the plane must be the same. Considering the properties of a tetrahedron, there are exactly 4 such planes (one for each vertex, where the plane is the plane that is parallel to the opposite face and equidistant from the vertex).

