A parallelepiped has 8 vertices. The median planes of a parallelepiped are the planes that are equidistant from pairs of opposite faces (since the vertices of a parallelepiped are symmetrically placed around the center of the parallelepiped). There are exactly 3 such planes, corresponding to the planes that are parallel to and equidistant from each pair of opposite faces.

