Then, evaluate the derivative at \(x = 1\):

\[ \left. \frac{dy}{dx} \right|_{x=1} = 2 \cdot 1^{-2/3} - \frac{4 \cdot 1^{-3/4}}{3} = 2 - \frac{4}{3} = \frac{6 - 4}{3} = \frac{2}{3} \]

So, the slope of the tangent line at \(x = 1\) is \(\frac{2}{3}\).

Finally, for step 3, use the point-slope form of the equation of a line \(y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)\), where \((x_1, y_1) = (1, \frac{2}{3})\) and \(m = \frac{2}{3}\).

