Given that \( a = \left\lfloor \log_{10} x \right\rfloor \) and \( b = \left\lfloor \log_{10} \frac{100}{x} \right\rfloor \), we can use the properties of logarithms to relate \( a \) and \( b \).

Using the change of base formula and logarithm properties:
\[ \log_{10} \frac{100}{x} = \log_{10} 100 - \log_{10} x = 2 - \log_{10} x. \]
Therefore,
\[ b = \left\lfloor 2 - \log_{10} x \right\rfloor = \left\lfloor 2 - a \right\rfloor. \]

