Combining the results from both inequalities, we get \(1 < x < 5\) and \(x \neq 3\). So, the natural numbers \(x\) that satisfy these conditions are \(2\) and \(4\).

Therefore, the natural values of \(x\) that satisfy the system of inequalities are \(2\) and \(4\).
